    "title": "FSU football injury update: WR Lawayne McCoy expects to play, Squirrel White questionable - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Peter Holland Jr. ,\n9 hours ago\nAs No. 9 Florida State football's return to the third game approaches, head coach Mike Norvell received positive news as he announced on Sept. 17 that wide receiver Lawayne McCoy will be available for the Sept. 20 game against Kent State , set for 3:30 p.m. at Doak Campbell Stadium.\nNorvell feels good about what he has seen from McCoy after missing time during camp. He even highlighted a touchdown pass on Tuesday, offering versatility in the wide receiver room.\n\"Lawayne got a great skill set where he can really play any of the receiver spots He's still going to have to work himself back into full game shape and just be real,\" Norvell said.\nNorvell also said that FSU will monitor his snap counts as he is still looking to get back in physical game shape.\nWhite's injury status remains questionable. He sustained an injury during the second quarter while on the punt return. He was spotted in his street clothes while wearing a brace on his left wrist on the sidelines.\nDuring fall camp, he was limited in action , but has been available in the first two games. He has two catches for 47 yards this season. His longest catch was a 40-yarder against Alabama .\n\"We'll see with Squirrel as it continues throughout this week, but I mean that was a good step for today, and just in regards to that,\" Norvell said.\nWhite has battled injuries throughout his career, including a PCL injury and an upper-body injury during his time at Tennessee.\nIf White is out, he will be the third starter who will miss time due to injury, joining running back Roydell Williams and Randy Pittman.\nMore: When is FSU football vs Kent State? Time, date, TV, prediction for Week 4 game\nKevin Wynn is getting closer to returning FSU defensive tackle Kevin Wynn may not be available against Kent State, but Norvell believes he is closer than usual to returning.\n\"He's close. I mean, let me say closer and so we're hopeful that here, even in these next couple of days, we'll be able to see the continued progress,\" Norvell said.\n\"Not anticipating him for Saturday, but looking that you next week could get into the conversation of it. So we'll see how it goes.\"\nWynn has not played in the last two games after his battle with injury during fall camp. The true freshman also turned heads during fall camp after being one of the top enrollees in the 2025 class.\nNeed a break Play the USA TODAY Daily Crossword Puzzle.\nHow to watch FSU vs. Kent State Date: Saturday, Time: Where: Doak Campbell Stadium, Tallahassee TV: Radio : Seminoles.com\nFlorida State football 2025 schedule Aug. 30, Alabama , W, 31-17 Sept. 6, East Texas A&M , 77-3 Sept. 20, Kent State, 3:30 p.m. Sept. 26, at Virginia (Friday), 7 p.m. Oct. 4, Miami , TBA Oct. 11, Pittsburgh , TBA Oct. 18, at Stanford, 10:30 p.m. Nov. 1 Wake Forest, TBA Nov. 8 at Clemson, TBA Nov. 15 Virginia Tech, TBA Nov. 21 at North Carolina State (Fri.), 8 p.m. Nov. 29 at Florida, TBA More: Florida State football's Tony White refuses to let defense rest on laurels of 2-0 start\nPeter Holland Jr. covers Florida State athletics for the Tallahassee Democrat. Contact him via email at PHolland@Gannett.com or on X @_Da_pistol.\nThis article originally appeared on Tallahassee Democrat: FSU football injury update: WR Lawayne McCoy expects to play, Squirrel White questionable",
